=== TEST 4: Calloc (Zero-initialized allocation) ===

Allocating array of 10 integers with calloc...
  Checking if memory is zeroed: YES - all zeros!

=== TEST 5: Realloc (Resize allocation) ===

Initial allocation of 100 bytes...
  Address: 0x100a4c8, Content: "Hello, World!"

Growing to 200 bytes with realloc...
  Address: 0x100a4c8, Content preserved: "Hello, World!"
  After append: "Hello, World! This is additional text after realloc."

Shrinking to 50 bytes with realloc...
  Address: 0x100a4c8, Content (truncated): "Hello, World! This is additional text after reall"

=== TEST 6: Edge Cases ===

Testing malloc(0)...
  Result: 0 (should be NULL)

Testing free(NULL)...
  No crash - good!

Testing realloc(NULL, 100) (should act like malloc)...
  Result: 0x100a4c8

Testing realloc(ptr, 0) (should act like free)...
  Allocated: 0x100a4c8
  After realloc(ptr, 0): 0 (should be NULL)

